From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim auf der Landwehr <tadl-git@taufderl.de>
Date: Sun, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build without mitmproxy-linux

mitmproxy-linux is the eBPF redirector for "mitmproxy --mode local". It
has no 32-bit ARM build. Drop it from the dependencies and do not import
it when the module loads; local mode still imports it lazily and then
fails with an ImportError, while all other modes work. Not submitted
upstream: it is only relevant on platforms upstream does not build
mitmproxy-linux for.

Signed-off-by: Tim auf der Landwehr <tadl-git@taufderl.de>
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -18,7 +18,6 @@ classifiers = [

 dependencies = [
     "mitmproxy_windows==0.12.15; os_name == 'nt'",
-    "mitmproxy_linux==0.12.15; sys_platform == 'linux'",
     "mitmproxy_macos==0.12.15; sys_platform == 'darwin'",
 ]

--- a/mitmproxy-rs/src/lib.rs
+++ b/mitmproxy-rs/src/lib.rs
@@ -123,8 +123,6 @@ fn init(m: &Bound<'_, PyModule>) -> PyResult<()> {
         // Import platform-specific modules here so that missing dependencies are raising immediately.
         #[cfg(target_os = "macos")]
         m.py().import("mitmproxy_macos")?;
-        #[cfg(all(target_os = "linux", not(feature = "docs")))]
-        m.py().import("mitmproxy_linux")?;
         #[cfg(windows)]
         m.py().import("mitmproxy_windows")?;
